IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `cpp-core`
IMPORT `cpp-core-calendar`
IMPORT `cpp-core-age`
IMPORT `cp3-nouns`

-- Canada Pension Plan Act, Part II -- THE UNADJUSTED PENSIONABLE EARNINGS OF A YEAR (sections 53 to 54.2).
--
-- Each year the Act sets three amounts for a contributor: the base unadjusted pensionable earnings
-- (section 53), the first additional ones (section 53.1, from 2019) and the second additional ones
-- (section 53.2, from 2024). Each is the least of three or four figures built from what the
-- contributor earned and contributed, and from what the Year's Maximum Pensionable Earnings, the
-- basic exemption and the contribution rates are. Sections 53.3 and 53.4 raise the amounts of a
-- contributor who was a family allowance recipient; sections 53.5 and 53.6 put the raised amounts
-- in place of the others; sections 54 to 54.2 adjust a year of division.
--
-- The figures of other sections (contributory salary and wages: section 12; contributory
-- self-employed earnings: section 13; salary and wages on which a contribution has been made: sections 15 to
-- 15.2; the maximum pensionable earnings, the additional maximum, the basic exemption and the contribution
-- rates: sections 11.1, 11.2, 16 to 20) are plain inputs, named after the fact and not the
-- section. Out of range: pieces cp1 (Part I, Division A and B).

§ `Part II -- Division B -- unadjusted pensionable earnings (sections 53 to 54.2)`

§§ `Helpers of this module (no provision licenses them)`

-- Not a provision: a contribution divided by a rate. The Act divides a contribution required for self-employed
-- earnings by the contribution rate for self-employed persons; a rate of zero gives no answer.
GIVEN contribution IS A NUMBER
      rate IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`cp3 — a contribution divided by a contribution rate` contribution rate MEANS
    IF rate EQUALS 0 THEN NOTHING ELSE JUST (contribution DIVIDED BY rate)

-- Not a provision: the greatest of a MAYBE NUMBER and nothing: NOTHING stays NOTHING.
GIVEN a IS A MAYBE NUMBER
      b IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`cp3 — the sum of two figures that may be missing` a b MEANS
    CONSIDER a
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST x THEN (CONSIDER b
                      WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
                      WHEN JUST y THEN JUST (x PLUS y))

§§ `53 -- base unadjusted pensionable earnings for a year`

-- src:1342 | 53 (1) Subject to section 54, the base unadjusted pensionable earnings of a contributor for a year are an amount equal to
-- src:1343 | (a) the aggregate of
-- src:1344 | (i) his contributory salary and wages for the year, and
-- src:1345 | (ii) his contributory self-employed earnings for the year in the case of an individual described in section 10,
-- src:1346 | (b) the aggregate of
-- src:1347 | (i) the contributor’s earnings on which a base contribution has been made for the year under this Act, calculated as the aggregate of
-- src:1348 | (A) the contributor’s salary and wages on which a base contribution has been made for the year, and
-- src:1349 | (B) the amount of any base contribution required to be made by the contributor for the year in respect of the contributor’s self-employed earnings divided by the contribution rate for self-employed persons for the year,
-- src:1350 | (ii) the contributor’s earnings on which a base contribution has been made for the year under a provincial pension plan, calculated as the aggregate of
-- src:1351 | (A) the amount that is determined in the prescribed manner to be the contributor’s salary and wages on which a base contribution has been made for the year by the contributor under a provincial pension plan, and
-- src:1352 | (B) the amount of any base contribution required to be made by the contributor for the year under a provincial pension plan in respect of the contributor’s self-employed earnings divided by the contribution rate for self-employed persons for the year, and
-- src:1353 | (iii) his basic exemption for the year, or
-- src:1354 | (c) his maximum pensionable earnings for the year,
-- src:1355 | whichever is the least, except that if the amount calculated as provided in paragraph (a) is equal to or less than the amount of the contributor’s basic exemption for the year, the contributor’s base unadjusted pensionable earnings for that year are deemed to be zero.
@ref Act s 53(1) (src:1342-1355)
GIVEN `the contributor's contributory salary and wages for the year` IS A NUMBER
      `the contributor is an individual described in section 10` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the contributor's contributory self-employed earnings for the year` IS A NUMBER
      `the contributor's salary and wages on which a base contribution has been made for the year` IS A NUMBER
      `the base contribution required to be made by the contributor for the year in respect of the contributor's self-employed earnings` IS A NUMBER
      `the amount determined in the prescribed manner to be the contributor's salary and wages on which a base contribution has been made for the year under a provincial pension plan` IS A NUMBER
      `the base contribution required to be made by the contributor for the year under a provincial pension plan in respect of the contributor's self-employed earnings` IS A NUMBER
      `the contribution rate for self-employed persons for the year` IS A NUMBER
      `the contributor's basic exemption for the year` IS A NUMBER
      `the contributor's maximum pensionable earnings for the year` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
-- Plain gloss: the base unadjusted pensionable earnings of a year are the least of (a) the year's
-- contributory salary and wages and, for a self-employed individual, contributory self-employed earnings,
-- (b) the earnings on which a base contribution was made (under this Act and under a provincial plan, the
-- self-employed contributions divided by the self-employed rate) plus the basic exemption, and (c) the
-- maximum pensionable earnings; but zero if (a) does not exceed the basic exemption.
-- The amount "determined in the prescribed manner" is regulation 41(1) (piece cr2), an input. Section 54
-- then adjusts the amount for a year of division. NOTHING means the self-employed rate is zero.
-- out of range: sections 10, 12, 13, 15, 18, 19 and 20 (piece cp1) and regulation 41 (piece cr2): the contributory salary and wages, the contributory self-employed earnings, the salary and wages on which a contribution was made, the contributions, the rate, the basic exemption and the maximum are taken as numbers.
`s 53(1) — the base unadjusted pensionable earnings of a contributor for a year` `the contributor's contributory salary and wages for the year` `the contributor is an individual described in section 10` `the contributor's contributory self-employed earnings for the year` `the contributor's salary and wages on which a base contribution has been made for the year` `the base contribution required to be made by the contributor for the year in respect of the contributor's self-employed earnings` `the amount determined in the prescribed manner to be the contributor's salary and wages on which a base contribution has been made for the year under a provincial pension plan` `the base contribution required to be made by the contributor for the year under a provincial pension plan in respect of the contributor's self-employed earnings` `the contribution rate for self-employed persons for the year` `the contributor's basic exemption for the year` `the contributor's maximum pensionable earnings for the year` MEANS
    IF `paragraph (a)` AT MOST `the contributor's basic exemption for the year`
    THEN JUST 0
    ELSE CONSIDER `paragraph (b)`
         WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
         WHEN JUST b THEN JUST (min (min `paragraph (a)` b) `the contributor's maximum pensionable earnings for the year`)
    WHERE
        `paragraph (a)` MEANS
            `the contributor's contributory salary and wages for the year` PLUS (IF `the contributor is an individual described in section 10` THEN `the contributor's contributory self-employed earnings for the year` ELSE 0)
        `subparagraph (b)(i)` MEANS
            `cp3 — the sum of two figures that may be missing`
                (JUST `the contributor's salary and wages on which a base contribution has been made for the year`)
                (`cp3 — a contribution divided by a contribution rate` `the base contribution required to be made by the contributor for the year in respect of the contributor's self-employed earnings` `the contribution rate for self-employed persons for the year`)
        `subparagraph (b)(ii)` MEANS
            `cp3 — the sum of two figures that may be missing`
                (JUST `the amount determined in the prescribed manner to be the contributor's salary and wages on which a base contribution has been made for the year under a provincial pension plan`)
                (`cp3 — a contribution divided by a contribution rate` `the base contribution required to be made by the contributor for the year under a provincial pension plan in respect of the contributor's self-employed earnings` `the contribution rate for self-employed persons for the year`)
        `paragraph (b)` MEANS
            `cp3 — the sum of two figures that may be missing`
                (`cp3 — the sum of two figures that may be missing` `subparagraph (b)(i)` `subparagraph (b)(ii)`)
                (JUST `the contributor's basic exemption for the year`)

-- src:1356 | Year in which retirement pension commences
-- src:1357 | (2) For the purposes of subsection (1), for the year in which a retirement pension becomes payable under this Act,
-- src:1358 | (a) the contributor’s basic exemption is equal to that proportion of the amount of the Year’s Basic Exemption that the number of months in the year that are not excluded from the contributory period — and are before the retirement pension becomes payable — is of 12; and
-- src:1359 | (b) the contributor’s maximum pensionable earnings is equal to that proportion of the amount of the Year’s Maximum Pensionable Earnings that the number of months in the year that are not excluded from the contributory period — and are before the retirement pension becomes payable — is of 12.
@ref Act s 53(2) (src:1356-1359)
GIVEN `the Year's Basic Exemption` IS A NUMBER
      `the number of months in the year that are not excluded from the contributory period and are before the retirement pension becomes payable` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
-- Plain gloss: for the year in which a retirement pension becomes payable, the contributor's basic
-- exemption is the Year's Basic Exemption times the months of the year before the pension, not excluded
-- from the contributory period, over 12.
`s 53(2)(a) — the contributor's basic exemption for the year in which a retirement pension becomes payable` `the Year's Basic Exemption` `the number of months in the year that are not excluded from the contributory period and are before the retirement pension becomes payable` MEANS
    `the Year's Basic Exemption` TIMES (`the number of months in the year that are not excluded from the contributory period and are before the retirement pension becomes payable` DIVIDED BY 12)

-- src:1356 | Year in which retirement pension commences
-- src:1357 | (2) For the purposes of subsection (1), for the year in which a retirement pension becomes payable under this Act,
-- src:1358 | (a) the contributor’s basic exemption is equal to that proportion of the amount of the Year’s Basic Exemption that the number of months in the year that are not excluded from the contributory period — and are before the retirement pension becomes payable — is of 12; and
-- src:1359 | (b) the contributor’s maximum pensionable earnings is equal to that proportion of the amount of the Year’s Maximum Pensionable Earnings that the number of months in the year that are not excluded from the contributory period — and are before the retirement pension becomes payable — is of 12.
@ref Act s 53(2) (src:1356-1359)
GIVEN `the Year's Maximum Pensionable Earnings` IS A NUMBER
      `the number of months in the year that are not excluded from the contributory period and are before the retirement pension becomes payable` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 53(2)(b) — the contributor's maximum pensionable earnings for the year in which a retirement pension becomes payable` `the Year's Maximum Pensionable Earnings` `the number of months in the year that are not excluded from the contributory period and are before the retirement pension becomes payable` MEANS
    `the Year's Maximum Pensionable Earnings` TIMES (`the number of months in the year that are not excluded from the contributory period and are before the retirement pension becomes payable` DIVIDED BY 12)

-- Not a provision: the months of a year that are before the month with which a retirement pension becomes payable
-- and are not excluded from the contributory period by reason of disability, the count that sections 53(2) uses.
GIVEN year IS A NUMBER
      events IS A `cp3 Life events of a contributor`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`cp3 — the months of a year before the retirement pension becomes payable that are not excluded` year events MEANS
    count (filter (GIVEN month YIELD `before the retirement pension` month AND (NOT (`excluded` month))) (`the twelve months`))
    WHERE
        `the twelve months` MEANS
            LIST (YearMonthDay year 1 1), (YearMonthDay year 2 1), (YearMonthDay year 3 1), (YearMonthDay year 4 1), (YearMonthDay year 5 1), (YearMonthDay year 6 1),
                 (YearMonthDay year 7 1), (YearMonthDay year 8 1), (YearMonthDay year 9 1), (YearMonthDay year 10 1), (YearMonthDay year 11 1), (YearMonthDay year 12 1)
        `before the retirement pension` month MEANS
            CONSIDER events's `the month with which a retirement pension becomes payable, if it does`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN TRUE
            WHEN JUST started THEN month LESS THAN `the month of a date` started
        `excluded` month MEANS
            any (GIVEN m YIELD `the month of a date` m EQUALS month) (events's `the months excluded from the contributory period by reason of disability`)

§§ `53.1 -- first additional unadjusted pensionable earnings for a year`

-- src:1361 | 53.1 (1) Subject to sections 53.5 and 54.1, for 2019 and each subsequent year, the first additional unadjusted pensionable earnings of a contributor for a year are an amount equal to the least of
-- src:1362 | (a) the aggregate of
-- src:1363 | (i) their contributory salary and wages for the year, and
-- src:1364 | (ii) their contributory self-employed earnings for the year in the case of an individual described in section 10,
-- src:1365 | (b) the aggregate of
-- src:1366 | (i) their earnings on which a first additional contribution has been made for the year calculated as the aggregate of
-- src:1367 | (A) their salary and wages on which a first additional contribution has been made for the year, and
-- src:1368 | (B) the amount of any first additional contribution required to be made by the contributor for the year in respect of the contributor’s self-employed earnings divided by the first additional contribution rate for self-employed persons for the year,
-- src:1369 | (ii) their earnings on which a first additional contribution has been made for the year under a provincial pension plan, calculated as the aggregate of
-- src:1370 | (A) the amount that is determined in the prescribed manner to be their salary and wages on which a first additional contribution has been made for the year by them under a provincial pension plan, and
-- src:1371 | (B) the amount of any first additional contribution required to be made by the contributor for the year under a provincial pension plan in respect of the contributor’s self-employed earnings divided by the first additional contribution rate for self-employed persons for the year, and
-- src:1372 | (iii) their basic exemption for the year, and
-- src:1373 | (c) their maximum pensionable earnings for the year.
-- src:1374 | However, if the amount calculated as provided in paragraph (a) is equal to or less than the amount of their basic exemption for the year, their first additional unadjusted pensionable earnings for that year are deemed to be zero.
@ref Act s 53.1(1) (src:1361-1374)
GIVEN `the contributor's contributory salary and wages for the year` IS A NUMBER
      `the contributor is an individual described in section 10` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the contributor's contributory self-employed earnings for the year` IS A NUMBER
      `the contributor's salary and wages on which a first additional contribution has been made for the year` IS A NUMBER
      `the first additional contribution required to be made by the contributor for the year in respect of the contributor's self-employed earnings` IS A NUMBER
      `the amount determined in the prescribed manner to be the contributor's salary and wages on which a first additional contribution has been made for the year under a provincial pension plan` IS A NUMBER
      `the first additional contribution required to be made by the contributor for the year under a provincial pension plan in respect of the contributor's self-employed earnings` IS A NUMBER
      `the first additional contribution rate for self-employed persons for the year` IS A NUMBER
      `the contributor's basic exemption for the year` IS A NUMBER
      `the contributor's maximum pensionable earnings for the year` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
-- Plain gloss: for 2019 and each later year, the least of (a) contributory salary and wages (and
-- self-employed earnings), (b) the earnings on which a first additional contribution was made plus the basic
-- exemption and (c) the maximum pensionable earnings; zero if (a) does not exceed the basic exemption.
-- out of range: sections 10, 12, 13, 15.1, 18, 19 and 20 (piece cp1) and regulation 41 (piece cr2): taken as numbers.
`s 53.1(1) — the first additional unadjusted pensionable earnings of a contributor for a year` `the contributor's contributory salary and wages for the year` `the contributor is an individual described in section 10` `the contributor's contributory self-employed earnings for the year` `the contributor's salary and wages on which a first additional contribution has been made for the year` `the first additional contribution required to be made by the contributor for the year in respect of the contributor's self-employed earnings` `the amount determined in the prescribed manner to be the contributor's salary and wages on which a first additional contribution has been made for the year under a provincial pension plan` `the first additional contribution required to be made by the contributor for the year under a provincial pension plan in respect of the contributor's self-employed earnings` `the first additional contribution rate for self-employed persons for the year` `the contributor's basic exemption for the year` `the contributor's maximum pensionable earnings for the year` MEANS
    IF `paragraph (a)` AT MOST `the contributor's basic exemption for the year`
    THEN JUST 0
    ELSE CONSIDER `paragraph (b)`
         WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
         WHEN JUST b THEN JUST (min (min `paragraph (a)` b) `the contributor's maximum pensionable earnings for the year`)
    WHERE
        `paragraph (a)` MEANS
            `the contributor's contributory salary and wages for the year` PLUS (IF `the contributor is an individual described in section 10` THEN `the contributor's contributory self-employed earnings for the year` ELSE 0)
        `subparagraph (b)(i)` MEANS
            `cp3 — the sum of two figures that may be missing`
                (JUST `the contributor's salary and wages on which a first additional contribution has been made for the year`)
                (`cp3 — a contribution divided by a contribution rate` `the first additional contribution required to be made by the contributor for the year in respect of the contributor's self-employed earnings` `the first additional contribution rate for self-employed persons for the year`)
        `subparagraph (b)(ii)` MEANS
            `cp3 — the sum of two figures that may be missing`
                (JUST `the amount determined in the prescribed manner to be the contributor's salary and wages on which a first additional contribution has been made for the year under a provincial pension plan`)
                (`cp3 — a contribution divided by a contribution rate` `the first additional contribution required to be made by the contributor for the year under a provincial pension plan in respect of the contributor's self-employed earnings` `the first additional contribution rate for self-employed persons for the year`)
        `paragraph (b)` MEANS
            `cp3 — the sum of two figures that may be missing`
                (`cp3 — the sum of two figures that may be missing` `subparagraph (b)(i)` `subparagraph (b)(ii)`)
                (JUST `the contributor's basic exemption for the year`)

-- src:1375 | Year in which retirement pension becomes payable
-- src:1376 | (2) For the purposes of subsection (1), for the year in which a retirement pension becomes payable under this Act,
-- src:1377 | (a) the contributor’s basic exemption is equal to that proportion of the amount of the Year’s Basic Exemption that the number of months in the year that are before the retirement pension becomes payable is of 12; and
-- src:1378 | (b) the contributor’s maximum pensionable earnings is equal to that proportion of the amount of the Year’s Maximum Pensionable Earnings that the number of months in the year that are before the retirement pension becomes payable is of 12.
@ref Act s 53.1(2) (src:1375-1378)
GIVEN `the Year's Basic Exemption` IS A NUMBER
      `the number of months in the year that are before the retirement pension becomes payable` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
-- Plain gloss: in the year a retirement pension becomes payable, the basic exemption is the Year's Basic Exemption
-- times the months before the pension over 12 (here no month is left out for disability).
`s 53.1(2)(a) — the contributor's basic exemption for the year in which a retirement pension becomes payable, for first additional earnings` `the Year's Basic Exemption` `the number of months in the year that are before the retirement pension becomes payable` MEANS
    `the Year's Basic Exemption` TIMES (`the number of months in the year that are before the retirement pension becomes payable` DIVIDED BY 12)

-- src:1375 | Year in which retirement pension becomes payable
-- src:1376 | (2) For the purposes of subsection (1), for the year in which a retirement pension becomes payable under this Act,
-- src:1377 | (a) the contributor’s basic exemption is equal to that proportion of the amount of the Year’s Basic Exemption that the number of months in the year that are before the retirement pension becomes payable is of 12; and
-- src:1378 | (b) the contributor’s maximum pensionable earnings is equal to that proportion of the amount of the Year’s Maximum Pensionable Earnings that the number of months in the year that are before the retirement pension becomes payable is of 12.
@ref Act s 53.1(2) (src:1375-1378)
GIVEN `the Year's Maximum Pensionable Earnings` IS A NUMBER
      `the number of months in the year that are before the retirement pension becomes payable` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 53.1(2)(b) — the contributor's maximum pensionable earnings for the year in which a retirement pension becomes payable, for first additional earnings` `the Year's Maximum Pensionable Earnings` `the number of months in the year that are before the retirement pension becomes payable` MEANS
    `the Year's Maximum Pensionable Earnings` TIMES (`the number of months in the year that are before the retirement pension becomes payable` DIVIDED BY 12)

§§ `53.2 -- second additional unadjusted pensionable earnings for a year`

-- src:1380 | 53.2 (1) Subject to sections 53.6 and 54.2, for 2024 and each subsequent year, the second additional unadjusted pensionable earnings of a contributor for a year are an amount equal to the least of
-- src:1381 | (a) the aggregate of
-- src:1382 | (i) the amount by which their contributory salary and wages for the year — not exceeding the contributor’s additional maximum pensionable earnings — exceeds the contributor’s maximum pensionable earnings,
-- src:1383 | (ii) in the case of an individual described in section 10, the amount by which their contributory self-employed earnings for the year — not exceeding the contributor’s additional maximum pensionable earnings — exceeds the contributor’s maximum pensionable earnings,
-- src:1384 | (b) their earnings on which a second additional contribution has been made for the year calculated as the aggregate of
-- src:1385 | (i) their salary and wages on which a second additional contribution has been made for the year,
-- src:1386 | (ii) their earnings on which a second additional contribution has been made for the year under a provincial pension plan, calculated as the aggregate of
-- src:1387 | (A) the amount that is determined in the prescribed manner to be their salary and wages on which a second additional contribution has been made for the year by them under a provincial pension plan, and
-- src:1388 | (B) the amount of any second additional contribution required to be made by the contributor for the year under a provincial pension plan in respect of the contributor’s self-employed earnings divided by the second additional contribution rate for self-employed persons for the year, and
-- src:1389 | (iii) the amount of any second additional contribution required to be made by the contributor for the year in respect of the contributor’s self-employed earnings divided by the second additional contribution rate for self-employed persons for the year, and
-- src:1390 | (c) the difference between the contributor’s additional maximum pensionable earnings and the contributor’s maximum pensionable earnings.
@ref Act s 53.2(1) (src:1380-1390)
GIVEN `the contributor's contributory salary and wages for the year` IS A NUMBER
      `the contributor is an individual described in section 10` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the contributor's contributory self-employed earnings for the year` IS A NUMBER
      `the contributor's salary and wages on which a second additional contribution has been made for the year` IS A NUMBER
      `the amount determined in the prescribed manner to be the contributor's salary and wages on which a second additional contribution has been made for the year under a provincial pension plan` IS A NUMBER
      `the second additional contribution required to be made by the contributor for the year under a provincial pension plan in respect of the contributor's self-employed earnings` IS A NUMBER
      `the second additional contribution required to be made by the contributor for the year in respect of the contributor's self-employed earnings` IS A NUMBER
      `the second additional contribution rate for self-employed persons for the year` IS A NUMBER
      `the contributor's maximum pensionable earnings for the year` IS A NUMBER
      `the contributor's additional maximum pensionable earnings for the year` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
-- Plain gloss: for 2024 and each later year, the least of (a) the part of the contributory salary and wages (and
-- self-employed earnings), not above the additional maximum, that is above the maximum pensionable earnings,
-- (b) the earnings on which a second additional contribution was made and (c) the additional maximum less the
-- maximum. Where the earnings do not reach the maximum there is no "amount by which" they exceed it: it is taken
-- as zero (NOTES.md, fork register). There is no zero rule and no basic exemption in this section.
-- out of range: sections 10, 12, 13, 15.2, 18 and 18.1 (piece cp1) and regulation 41 (piece cr2): taken as numbers.
`s 53.2(1) — the second additional unadjusted pensionable earnings of a contributor for a year` `the contributor's contributory salary and wages for the year` `the contributor is an individual described in section 10` `the contributor's contributory self-employed earnings for the year` `the contributor's salary and wages on which a second additional contribution has been made for the year` `the amount determined in the prescribed manner to be the contributor's salary and wages on which a second additional contribution has been made for the year under a provincial pension plan` `the second additional contribution required to be made by the contributor for the year under a provincial pension plan in respect of the contributor's self-employed earnings` `the second additional contribution required to be made by the contributor for the year in respect of the contributor's self-employed earnings` `the second additional contribution rate for self-employed persons for the year` `the contributor's maximum pensionable earnings for the year` `the contributor's additional maximum pensionable earnings for the year` MEANS
    CONSIDER `paragraph (b)`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST b THEN JUST (min (min `paragraph (a)` b) (`the contributor's additional maximum pensionable earnings for the year` MINUS `the contributor's maximum pensionable earnings for the year`))
    WHERE
        `the amount by which earnings not exceeding the additional maximum exceed the maximum` earnings MEANS
            max 0 ((min earnings `the contributor's additional maximum pensionable earnings for the year`) MINUS `the contributor's maximum pensionable earnings for the year`)
        `paragraph (a)` MEANS
            `the amount by which earnings not exceeding the additional maximum exceed the maximum` `the contributor's contributory salary and wages for the year`
            PLUS (IF `the contributor is an individual described in section 10` THEN `the amount by which earnings not exceeding the additional maximum exceed the maximum` `the contributor's contributory self-employed earnings for the year` ELSE 0)
        `subparagraph (b)(ii)` MEANS
            `cp3 — the sum of two figures that may be missing`
                (JUST `the amount determined in the prescribed manner to be the contributor's salary and wages on which a second additional contribution has been made for the year under a provincial pension plan`)
                (`cp3 — a contribution divided by a contribution rate` `the second additional contribution required to be made by the contributor for the year under a provincial pension plan in respect of the contributor's self-employed earnings` `the second additional contribution rate for self-employed persons for the year`)
        `paragraph (b)` MEANS
            `cp3 — the sum of two figures that may be missing`
                (`cp3 — the sum of two figures that may be missing` (JUST `the contributor's salary and wages on which a second additional contribution has been made for the year`) `subparagraph (b)(ii)`)
                (`cp3 — a contribution divided by a contribution rate` `the second additional contribution required to be made by the contributor for the year in respect of the contributor's self-employed earnings` `the second additional contribution rate for self-employed persons for the year`)

-- src:1391 | Year in which retirement pension becomes payable
-- src:1392 | (2) For the purposes of subsection (1), for the year in which a retirement pension becomes payable under this Act,
-- src:1393 | (a) the contributor’s maximum pensionable earnings is equal to that proportion of the amount of the Year’s Maximum Pensionable Earnings that the number of months in the year that are before the retirement pension becomes payable is of 12; and
-- src:1394 | (b) the contributor’s additional maximum pensionable earnings is equal to that proportion of the amount of the Year’s Additional Maximum Pensionable Earnings that the number of months in the year that are before the retirement pension becomes payable is of 12.
@ref Act s 53.2(2) (src:1391-1394)
GIVEN `the Year's Maximum Pensionable Earnings` IS A NUMBER
      `the number of months in the year that are before the retirement pension becomes payable` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
-- Plain gloss: in the year a retirement pension becomes payable, the maximum pensionable earnings and the additional
-- maximum pensionable earnings are each the Year's figure times the months before the pension over 12.
`s 53.2(2)(a) — the contributor's maximum pensionable earnings for the year in which a retirement pension becomes payable, for second additional earnings` `the Year's Maximum Pensionable Earnings` `the number of months in the year that are before the retirement pension becomes payable` MEANS
    `the Year's Maximum Pensionable Earnings` TIMES (`the number of months in the year that are before the retirement pension becomes payable` DIVIDED BY 12)

-- src:1391 | Year in which retirement pension becomes payable
-- src:1392 | (2) For the purposes of subsection (1), for the year in which a retirement pension becomes payable under this Act,
-- src:1393 | (a) the contributor’s maximum pensionable earnings is equal to that proportion of the amount of the Year’s Maximum Pensionable Earnings that the number of months in the year that are before the retirement pension becomes payable is of 12; and
-- src:1394 | (b) the contributor’s additional maximum pensionable earnings is equal to that proportion of the amount of the Year’s Additional Maximum Pensionable Earnings that the number of months in the year that are before the retirement pension becomes payable is of 12.
@ref Act s 53.2(2) (src:1391-1394)
GIVEN `the Year's Additional Maximum Pensionable Earnings` IS A NUMBER
      `the number of months in the year that are before the retirement pension becomes payable` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 53.2(2)(b) — the contributor's additional maximum pensionable earnings for the year in which a retirement pension becomes payable` `the Year's Additional Maximum Pensionable Earnings` `the number of months in the year that are before the retirement pension becomes payable` MEANS
    `the Year's Additional Maximum Pensionable Earnings` TIMES (`the number of months in the year that are before the retirement pension becomes payable` DIVIDED BY 12)

§§ `53.3 -- amount attributed to a family allowance recipient, first additional contributory period`

-- Not a provision: the Year's Maximum Pensionable Earnings of a year before the family allowance year, prorated by the
-- months of the additional contributory period when that period begins in the year (sections 53.3(5) and 53.4(4)).
GIVEN year IS A `cp3 Year in a family allowance lookback`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`cp3 — the Year's Maximum Pensionable Earnings of a year before the family allowance year, prorated if the additional contributory period begins in it` year MEANS
    IF year's `the additional contributory period begins in that year before`
    THEN (year's `Year's Maximum Pensionable Earnings for that year before`) TIMES ((year's `months of that year before in the additional contributory period`) DIVIDED BY 12)
    ELSE year's `Year's Maximum Pensionable Earnings for that year before`

-- Not a provision: the same for the Year's Additional Maximum Pensionable Earnings (section 53.4(4)(b)).
GIVEN year IS A `cp3 Year in a family allowance lookback`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`cp3 — the Year's Additional Maximum Pensionable Earnings of a year before the family allowance year, prorated if the additional contributory period begins in it` year MEANS
    IF year's `the additional contributory period begins in that year before`
    THEN (year's `Year's Additional Maximum Pensionable Earnings for that year before`) TIMES ((year's `months of that year before in the additional contributory period`) DIVIDED BY 12)
    ELSE year's `Year's Additional Maximum Pensionable Earnings for that year before`

-- Not a provision: A to E of section 53.3(1): the year's first additional unadjusted pensionable earnings divided by its
-- Year's Maximum Pensionable Earnings (prorated by subsection (5) where it applies); a zero denominator has no months, so
-- the ratio is taken as zero.
GIVEN year IS A `cp3 Year in a family allowance lookback`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`cp3 — the ratio of a year before the family allowance year, first additional` year MEANS
    IF `the denominator` EQUALS 0 THEN 0 ELSE (year's `additional unadjusted pensionable earnings for that year before`) DIVIDED BY `the denominator`
    WHERE
        `the denominator` MEANS `cp3 — the Year's Maximum Pensionable Earnings of a year before the family allowance year, prorated if the additional contributory period begins in it` year

-- Not a provision: A to E of section 53.4(1): the same, divided by the difference between the Year's Additional Maximum
-- Pensionable Earnings and the Year's Maximum Pensionable Earnings, each prorated as subsection (4) says.
GIVEN year IS A `cp3 Year in a family allowance lookback`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`cp3 — the ratio of a year before the family allowance year, second additional` year MEANS
    IF `the denominator` EQUALS 0 THEN 0 ELSE (year's `additional unadjusted pensionable earnings for that year before`) DIVIDED BY `the denominator`
    WHERE
        `the denominator` MEANS
            (`cp3 — the Year's Additional Maximum Pensionable Earnings of a year before the family allowance year, prorated if the additional contributory period begins in it` year)
            MINUS (`cp3 — the Year's Maximum Pensionable Earnings of a year before the family allowance year, prorated if the additional contributory period begins in it` year)

-- src:1396 | 53.3 (1) An amount, determined by the following formula, shall be attributed to a contributor for a year during which they were a family allowance recipient with respect to one child, if that amount is greater than their first additional unadjusted pensionable earnings for that year and is greater than their basic exemption for the year:
-- src:1397 | [[(M1 × A) + (M2 × B) + (M3 × C) + (M4 × D) + (M5 × E) + (M6 × F) + Q]/R] × T
-- src:1398 | where
-- src:1399 | A is the first additional unadjusted pensionable earnings of the contributor for the fifth year before the year in which the contributor became a family allowance recipient with respect to the child, divided by the Year’s Maximum Pensionable Earnings for that fifth year;
-- src:1400 | B is the first additional unadjusted pensionable earnings of the contributor for the fourth year before the year in which the contributor became a family allowance recipient with respect to the child, divided by the Year’s Maximum Pensionable Earnings for that fourth year;
-- src:1401 | C is the first additional unadjusted pensionable earnings of the contributor for the third year before the year in which the contributor became a family allowance recipient with respect to the child, divided by the Year’s Maximum Pensionable Earnings for that third year;
-- src:1402 | D is the first additional unadjusted pensionable earnings of the contributor for the second year before the year in which the contributor became a family allowance recipient with respect to the child, divided by the Year’s Maximum Pensionable Earnings for that second year;
-- src:1403 | E is the first additional unadjusted pensionable earnings of the contributor for the year before the year in which the contributor became a family allowance recipient with respect to the child, divided by the Year’s Maximum Pensionable Earnings for that prior year;
-- src:1404 | F is,
-- src:1405 | (a) in the case where an amount has been previously attributed by this section for the year in which the contributor became a family allowance recipient with respect to the child, that amount, or
-- src:1406 | (b) in any other case,
-- src:1407 | (i) if the contributor became a family allowance recipient with respect to the child in January, zero, or
-- src:1408 | (ii) in any other case, the lesser of 1 and the number determined by the formula
-- src:1409 | G/[H × (M6/12)]
-- src:1410 | where
-- src:1411 | G is the first additional unadjusted pensionable earnings of the contributor for the year in which the contributor became a family allowance recipient with respect to the child, and
-- src:1412 | H is the Year’s Maximum Pensionable Earnings for the year in which the contributor became a family allowance recipient with respect to the child;
-- src:1413 | M1 is the lesser of
-- src:1414 | (a) the number of months in the contributor’s first additional contributory period in the fifth year before the year in which the contributor became a family allowance recipient with respect to the child, and
-- src:1415 | (b) the number determined by the formula
-- src:1416 | 12 − M6
-- src:1417 | M2 is the number of months in the contributor’s first additional contributory period in the fourth year before the year in which the contributor became a family allowance recipient with respect to the child;
-- src:1418 | M3 is the number of months in the contributor’s first additional contributory period in the third year before the year in which the contributor became a family allowance recipient with respect to the child;
-- src:1419 | M4 is the number of months in the contributor’s first additional contributory period in the second year before the year in which the contributor became a family allowance recipient with respect to the child;
-- src:1420 | M5 is the number of months in the contributor’s first additional contributory period in the year before the year in which the contributor became a family allowance recipient with respect to the child;
-- src:1421 | M6 is the number of months in the contributor’s first additional contributory period in the year in which the contributor became a family allowance recipient with respect to the child that are before the month in which they became a family allowance recipient with respect to that child;
-- src:1422 | Q is, as the case may be,
-- src:1423 | (a) if the sum of M1, M2, M3, M4, M5 and M6 is less than 36, the number determined by the formula
-- src:1424 | [36 − (M1 + M2 + M3 + M4 + M5 + M6)] × 0.4
-- src:1425 | (b) in any other case, zero;
-- src:1426 | R is the greater of 36 and the sum of M1, M2, M3, M4, M5 and M6; and
-- src:1427 | T is the Year’s Maximum Pensionable Earnings for the year for which the amount is to be attributed.
@ref Act s 53.3(1) (src:1396-1427)
GIVEN `the fifth year before the year in which the contributor became a family allowance recipient with respect to the child` IS A `cp3 Year in a family allowance lookback`
      `the fourth year before` IS A `cp3 Year in a family allowance lookback`
      `the third year before` IS A `cp3 Year in a family allowance lookback`
      `the second year before` IS A `cp3 Year in a family allowance lookback`
      `the year before` IS A `cp3 Year in a family allowance lookback`
      `the contributor's first additional unadjusted pensionable earnings for the year in which they became a family allowance recipient with respect to the child (G)` IS A NUMBER
      `the Year's Maximum Pensionable Earnings for the year in which they became a family allowance recipient with respect to the child (H)` IS A NUMBER
      `the number of months in the first additional contributory period in the year in which they became a family allowance recipient that are before the month in which they became one (M6)` IS A NUMBER
      `the contributor became a family allowance recipient with respect to the child in January` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the amount previously attributed by this section for the year in which they became a family allowance recipient with respect to the child` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
      `the Year's Maximum Pensionable Earnings for the year for which the amount is to be attributed (T)` IS A NUMBER
      `the contributor's first additional unadjusted pensionable earnings for the year for which the amount is to be attributed` IS A NUMBER
      `the contributor's basic exemption for the year for which the amount is to be attributed` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
-- Plain gloss: a contributor who was a family allowance recipient for one child is attributed, for a year in which
-- that is so, an amount worked out from the first additional unadjusted pensionable earnings of the five years before the
-- year they became a recipient and of that year, weighted by the months of the additional contributory period in each, with
-- 36 months as the least weight (months short of 36 count as 0.4 each), times the Year's Maximum Pensionable Earnings of the
-- year of attribution. The amount is attributed only if it is greater than the contributor's first additional unadjusted
-- pensionable earnings and greater than the basic exemption for that year; NOTHING means no amount is attributed.
-- F (a) is "that amount" as written: the amount previously attributed, taken as it stands in the formula. The text sets it
-- beside ratios (A to E) and does not say whether it is a ratio (NOTES.md, fork register).
-- out of range: the Family Allowances Act (another statute, not among the inputs) and regulation 77 (piece cr2): the year in which the contributor became a family allowance recipient is taken as a fact.
`s 53.3(1) — the amount attributed to a family allowance recipient for a year, first additional contributory period, for one child` `the fifth year before the year in which the contributor became a family allowance recipient with respect to the child` `the fourth year before` `the third year before` `the second year before` `the year before` `the contributor's first additional unadjusted pensionable earnings for the year in which they became a family allowance recipient with respect to the child (G)` `the Year's Maximum Pensionable Earnings for the year in which they became a family allowance recipient with respect to the child (H)` `the number of months in the first additional contributory period in the year in which they became a family allowance recipient that are before the month in which they became one (M6)` `the contributor became a family allowance recipient with respect to the child in January` `the amount previously attributed by this section for the year in which they became a family allowance recipient with respect to the child` `the Year's Maximum Pensionable Earnings for the year for which the amount is to be attributed (T)` `the contributor's first additional unadjusted pensionable earnings for the year for which the amount is to be attributed` `the contributor's basic exemption for the year for which the amount is to be attributed` MEANS
    IF `the amount` GREATER THAN `the contributor's first additional unadjusted pensionable earnings for the year for which the amount is to be attributed` AND `the amount` GREATER THAN `the contributor's basic exemption for the year for which the amount is to be attributed`
    THEN JUST `the amount`
    ELSE NOTHING
    WHERE
        M6 MEANS `the number of months in the first additional contributory period in the year in which they became a family allowance recipient that are before the month in which they became one (M6)`
        M1 MEANS min (`the fifth year before the year in which the contributor became a family allowance recipient with respect to the child`'s `months of that year before in the additional contributory period`) (12 MINUS M6)
        M2 MEANS `the fourth year before`'s `months of that year before in the additional contributory period`
        M3 MEANS `the third year before`'s `months of that year before in the additional contributory period`
        M4 MEANS `the second year before`'s `months of that year before in the additional contributory period`
        M5 MEANS `the year before`'s `months of that year before in the additional contributory period`
        `the sum of M1 to M6` MEANS M1 PLUS M2 PLUS M3 PLUS M4 PLUS M5 PLUS M6
        `A` MEANS `cp3 — the ratio of a year before the family allowance year, first additional` `the fifth year before the year in which the contributor became a family allowance recipient with respect to the child`
        B MEANS `cp3 — the ratio of a year before the family allowance year, first additional` `the fourth year before`
        C MEANS `cp3 — the ratio of a year before the family allowance year, first additional` `the third year before`
        D MEANS `cp3 — the ratio of a year before the family allowance year, first additional` `the second year before`
        E MEANS `cp3 — the ratio of a year before the family allowance year, first additional` `the year before`
        F MEANS
            CONSIDER `the amount previously attributed by this section for the year in which they became a family allowance recipient with respect to the child`
            WHEN JUST previous THEN previous
            WHEN NOTHING THEN
                IF `the contributor became a family allowance recipient with respect to the child in January`
                THEN 0
                ELSE (IF M6 EQUALS 0 OR `the Year's Maximum Pensionable Earnings for the year in which they became a family allowance recipient with respect to the child (H)` EQUALS 0
                      THEN 0
                      ELSE min 1 (`the contributor's first additional unadjusted pensionable earnings for the year in which they became a family allowance recipient with respect to the child (G)` DIVIDED BY (`the Year's Maximum Pensionable Earnings for the year in which they became a family allowance recipient with respect to the child (H)` TIMES (M6 DIVIDED BY 12))))
        Q MEANS
            IF `the sum of M1 to M6` LESS THAN 36 THEN (36 MINUS `the sum of M1 to M6`) TIMES 0.4 ELSE 0
        R MEANS max 36 `the sum of M1 to M6`
        `the amount` MEANS
            ((((M1 TIMES `A`) PLUS (M2 TIMES B) PLUS (M3 TIMES C) PLUS (M4 TIMES D) PLUS (M5 TIMES E) PLUS (M6 TIMES F)) PLUS Q) DIVIDED BY R) TIMES `the Year's Maximum Pensionable Earnings for the year for which the amount is to be attributed (T)`

-- src:1429 | (2) If the contributor is a family allowance recipient with respect to more than one child in a year, an amount shall be attributed to the contributor for that year that is the greater of each amount determined under subsection (1), calculated with respect to each child without regard to the other children.
@ref Act s 53.3(2) (src:1429)
GIVEN `the amounts determined under subsection (1), one for each child, calculated without regard to the other children` IS A LIST OF NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
-- Plain gloss: a recipient for more than one child is attributed the greater of the amounts worked out for each child.
-- NOTHING means there is no amount.
`s 53.3(2) — the amount attributed to a family allowance recipient for more than one child, first additional contributory period` `the amounts determined under subsection (1), one for each child, calculated without regard to the other children` MEANS
    IF null `the amounts determined under subsection (1), one for each child, calculated without regard to the other children`
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE JUST (maximum `the amounts determined under subsection (1), one for each child, calculated without regard to the other children`)

-- src:1431 | (3) For the purposes of subsection (1), for the year in which a retirement pension becomes payable under this Act, the contributor’s basic exemption is equal to that proportion of the amount of the Year’s Basic Exemption that the number of months in the year that are before the retirement pension becomes payable is of 12.
@ref Act s 53.3(3) (src:1431)
GIVEN `the Year's Basic Exemption` IS A NUMBER
      `the number of months in the year that are before the retirement pension becomes payable` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 53.3(3) — the contributor's basic exemption for the year in which a retirement pension becomes payable, for the attribution` `the Year's Basic Exemption` `the number of months in the year that are before the retirement pension becomes payable` MEANS
    `the Year's Basic Exemption` TIMES (`the number of months in the year that are before the retirement pension becomes payable` DIVIDED BY 12)

-- src:1433 | (4) For the purposes of subsection (1), for a year in which the contributor’s first additional contributory period begins or ends, the amount to be attributed to the contributor is equal to that proportion of the amount determined in accordance with subsection (1) that the number of months that are included in the contributor’s first additional contributory period in that year is of 12.
@ref Act s 53.3(4) (src:1433)
GIVEN `the amount determined in accordance with subsection (1)` IS A NUMBER
      `the number of months included in the first additional contributory period in the year` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
-- Plain gloss: for a year in which the first additional contributory period begins or ends, the amount attributed is the
-- share of the subsection (1) amount that the months of the period in the year are of 12.
`s 53.3(4) — the amount attributed for a year in which the first additional contributory period begins or ends` `the amount determined in accordance with subsection (1)` `the number of months included in the first additional contributory period in the year` MEANS
    `the amount determined in accordance with subsection (1)` TIMES (`the number of months included in the first additional contributory period in the year` DIVIDED BY 12)

-- src:1435 | (5) For the purposes of the descriptions of A to E in subsection (1), if the contributor’s first additional contributory period begins in the five years before the year in which they became a family allowance recipient, the Year’s Maximum Pensionable Earnings for the year in which their first additional contributory period begins is replaced by the prorated portion determined by the formula
-- src:1436 | A × (M ÷ 12)
-- src:1437 | where
-- src:1438 | A is the Year’s Maximum Pensionable Earnings for the year in which the contributor’s first additional contributory period begins; and
-- src:1439 | M is the number of months in that year that are included in the contributor’s first additional contributory period.
@ref Act s 53.3(5) (src:1435-1439)
GIVEN `the Year's Maximum Pensionable Earnings for the year in which the first additional contributory period begins (A)` IS A NUMBER
      `the number of months in that year that are included in the first additional contributory period (M)` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
-- Plain gloss: for the descriptions of A to E of subsection (1), when the period begins in one of the five years before
-- the year they became a family allowance recipient, that year's Year's Maximum Pensionable Earnings is replaced by A x (M / 12).
-- The formula of subsection (1) makes this replacement itself, from the lookback record's field.
`s 53.3(5) — the Year's Maximum Pensionable Earnings replaced for the year in which the first additional contributory period begins` `the Year's Maximum Pensionable Earnings for the year in which the first additional contributory period begins (A)` `the number of months in that year that are included in the first additional contributory period (M)` MEANS
    `the Year's Maximum Pensionable Earnings for the year in which the first additional contributory period begins (A)` TIMES (`the number of months in that year that are included in the first additional contributory period (M)` DIVIDED BY 12)

§§ `53.4 -- amount attributed to a family allowance recipient, second additional contributory period`

-- src:1441 | 53.4 (1) An amount, determined by the following formula, shall be attributed to a contributor for a year during which they were a family allowance recipient with respect to one child, if that amount is greater than their second additional unadjusted pensionable earnings for that year:
-- src:1442 | [[(M1 × A) + (M2 × B) + (M3 × C) + (M4 × D) + (M5 × E) + (M6 × F)]/R] × T
-- src:1443 | where
-- src:1444 | A is the second additional unadjusted pensionable earnings of the contributor for the fifth year before the year in which the contributor became a family allowance recipient with respect to the child, divided by the difference between the Year’s Additional Maximum Pensionable Earnings and the Year’s Maximum Pensionable Earnings, for that fifth year;
-- src:1445 | B is the second additional unadjusted pensionable earnings of the contributor for the fourth year before the year in which the contributor became a family allowance recipient with respect to the child, divided by the difference between the Year’s Additional Maximum Pensionable Earnings and the Year’s Maximum Pensionable Earnings for that fourth year;
-- src:1446 | C is the second additional unadjusted pensionable earnings of the contributor for the third year before the year in which the contributor became a family allowance recipient with respect to the child, divided by the difference between the Year’s Additional Maximum Pensionable Earnings and the Year’s Maximum Pensionable Earnings for that third year;
-- src:1447 | D is the second additional unadjusted pensionable earnings of the contributor for the second year before the year in which the contributor became a family allowance recipient with respect to the child, divided by the difference between the Year’s Additional Maximum Pensionable Earnings and the Year’s Maximum Pensionable Earnings for that second year;
-- src:1448 | E is the second additional unadjusted pensionable earnings of the contributor for the year before the year in which the contributor became a family allowance recipient with respect to the child, divided by the difference between the Year’s Additional Maximum Pensionable Earnings and the Year’s Maximum Pensionable Earnings for that prior year;
-- src:1449 | F is,
-- src:1450 | (a) in the case where an amount has been previously attributed by this section for the year in which the contributor became a family allowance recipient with respect to the child, that amount, or
-- src:1451 | (b) in any other case
-- src:1452 | (i) if the contributor became a family allowance recipient with respect to the child in January, zero, or
-- src:1453 | (ii) in any other case, the lesser of 1 and the number determined by the formula
-- src:1454 | G/[H × (M6/12)]
-- src:1455 | where
-- src:1456 | G is the second additional unadjusted pensionable earnings of the contributor for the year in which the contributor became a family allowance recipient with respect to the child, and
-- src:1457 | H is the difference between the Year’s Additional Maximum Pensionable Earnings and the Year’s Maximum Pensionable Earnings for the year in which the contributor became a family allowance recipient with respect to the child;
-- src:1458 | M1 is the lesser of
-- src:1459 | (a) the number of months in the contributor’s second additional contributory period in the fifth year before the year in which the contributor became a family allowance recipient with respect to the child, and
-- src:1460 | (b) the number determined by the formula
-- src:1461 | 12 − M6
-- src:1462 | M2 is the number of months in the contributor’s second additional contributory period in the fourth year before the year in which the contributor became a family allowance recipient with respect to the child;
-- src:1463 | M3 is the number of months in the contributor’s second additional contributory period in the third year before the year in which the contributor became a family allowance recipient with respect to the child;
-- src:1464 | M4 is the number of months in the contributor’s second additional contributory period in the second year before the year in which the contributor became a family allowance recipient with respect to the child;
-- src:1465 | M5 is the number of months in the contributor’s second additional contributory period in the year before the year in which the contributor became a family allowance recipient with respect to the child;
-- src:1466 | M6 is the number of months in the contributor’s second additional contributory period in the year in which the contributor became a family allowance recipient with respect to the child that are before the month in which they became a family allowance recipient with respect to that child;
-- src:1467 | R is the greater of 36 and the sum of M1, M2, M3, M4, M5 and M6; and
-- src:1468 | T is the difference between the Year’s Additional Maximum Pensionable Earnings and the Year’s Maximum Pensionable Earnings for the year for which the amount is to be attributed.
@ref Act s 53.4(1) (src:1441-1468)
GIVEN `the fifth year before the year in which the contributor became a family allowance recipient with respect to the child` IS A `cp3 Year in a family allowance lookback`
      `the fourth year before` IS A `cp3 Year in a family allowance lookback`
      `the third year before` IS A `cp3 Year in a family allowance lookback`
      `the second year before` IS A `cp3 Year in a family allowance lookback`
      `the year before` IS A `cp3 Year in a family allowance lookback`
      `the contributor's second additional unadjusted pensionable earnings for the year in which they became a family allowance recipient with respect to the child (G)` IS A NUMBER
      `the difference between the Year's Additional Maximum Pensionable Earnings and the Year's Maximum Pensionable Earnings for the year in which they became a family allowance recipient with respect to the child (H)` IS A NUMBER
      `the number of months in the second additional contributory period in the year in which they became a family allowance recipient that are before the month in which they became one (M6)` IS A NUMBER
      `the contributor became a family allowance recipient with respect to the child in January` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the amount previously attributed by this section for the year in which they became a family allowance recipient with respect to the child` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
      `the difference between the Year's Additional Maximum Pensionable Earnings and the Year's Maximum Pensionable Earnings for the year for which the amount is to be attributed (T)` IS A NUMBER
      `the contributor's second additional unadjusted pensionable earnings for the year for which the amount is to be attributed` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
-- Plain gloss: the same as section 53.3(1) for the second additional contributory period, with the Year's Additional
-- Maximum Pensionable Earnings less the Year's Maximum Pensionable Earnings in place of the Year's Maximum Pensionable
-- Earnings, no filler of 0.4 a month, and the amount attributed only if greater than the second additional unadjusted
-- pensionable earnings of the year (there is no basic exemption test here). In the lookback records the
-- `additional` fields are the second additional ones. NOTHING means no amount is attributed.
`s 53.4(1) — the amount attributed to a family allowance recipient for a year, second additional contributory period, for one child` `the fifth year before the year in which the contributor became a family allowance recipient with respect to the child` `the fourth year before` `the third year before` `the second year before` `the year before` `the contributor's second additional unadjusted pensionable earnings for the year in which they became a family allowance recipient with respect to the child (G)` `the difference between the Year's Additional Maximum Pensionable Earnings and the Year's Maximum Pensionable Earnings for the year in which they became a family allowance recipient with respect to the child (H)` `the number of months in the second additional contributory period in the year in which they became a family allowance recipient that are before the month in which they became one (M6)` `the contributor became a family allowance recipient with respect to the child in January` `the amount previously attributed by this section for the year in which they became a family allowance recipient with respect to the child` `the difference between the Year's Additional Maximum Pensionable Earnings and the Year's Maximum Pensionable Earnings for the year for which the amount is to be attributed (T)` `the contributor's second additional unadjusted pensionable earnings for the year for which the amount is to be attributed` MEANS
    IF `the amount` GREATER THAN `the contributor's second additional unadjusted pensionable earnings for the year for which the amount is to be attributed`
    THEN JUST `the amount`
    ELSE NOTHING
    WHERE
        M6 MEANS `the number of months in the second additional contributory period in the year in which they became a family allowance recipient that are before the month in which they became one (M6)`
        M1 MEANS min (`the fifth year before the year in which the contributor became a family allowance recipient with respect to the child`'s `months of that year before in the additional contributory period`) (12 MINUS M6)
        M2 MEANS `the fourth year before`'s `months of that year before in the additional contributory period`
        M3 MEANS `the third year before`'s `months of that year before in the additional contributory period`
        M4 MEANS `the second year before`'s `months of that year before in the additional contributory period`
        M5 MEANS `the year before`'s `months of that year before in the additional contributory period`
        `the sum of M1 to M6` MEANS M1 PLUS M2 PLUS M3 PLUS M4 PLUS M5 PLUS M6
        `A` MEANS `cp3 — the ratio of a year before the family allowance year, second additional` `the fifth year before the year in which the contributor became a family allowance recipient with respect to the child`
        B MEANS `cp3 — the ratio of a year before the family allowance year, second additional` `the fourth year before`
        C MEANS `cp3 — the ratio of a year before the family allowance year, second additional` `the third year before`
        D MEANS `cp3 — the ratio of a year before the family allowance year, second additional` `the second year before`
        E MEANS `cp3 — the ratio of a year before the family allowance year, second additional` `the year before`
        F MEANS
            CONSIDER `the amount previously attributed by this section for the year in which they became a family allowance recipient with respect to the child`
            WHEN JUST previous THEN previous
            WHEN NOTHING THEN
                IF `the contributor became a family allowance recipient with respect to the child in January`
                THEN 0
                ELSE (IF M6 EQUALS 0 OR `the difference between the Year's Additional Maximum Pensionable Earnings and the Year's Maximum Pensionable Earnings for the year in which they became a family allowance recipient with respect to the child (H)` EQUALS 0
                      THEN 0
                      ELSE min 1 (`the contributor's second additional unadjusted pensionable earnings for the year in which they became a family allowance recipient with respect to the child (G)` DIVIDED BY (`the difference between the Year's Additional Maximum Pensionable Earnings and the Year's Maximum Pensionable Earnings for the year in which they became a family allowance recipient with respect to the child (H)` TIMES (M6 DIVIDED BY 12))))
        R MEANS max 36 `the sum of M1 to M6`
        `the amount` MEANS
            (((M1 TIMES `A`) PLUS (M2 TIMES B) PLUS (M3 TIMES C) PLUS (M4 TIMES D) PLUS (M5 TIMES E) PLUS (M6 TIMES F)) DIVIDED BY R) TIMES `the difference between the Year's Additional Maximum Pensionable Earnings and the Year's Maximum Pensionable Earnings for the year for which the amount is to be attributed (T)`

-- src:1470 | (2) If the contributor is a family allowance recipient with respect to more than one child in a year, an amount shall be attributed to the contributor for that year that is the greater of each amount determined under subsection (1), calculated with respect to each child without regard to the other children.
@ref Act s 53.4(2) (src:1470)
GIVEN `the amounts determined under subsection (1), one for each child, calculated without regard to the other children` IS A LIST OF NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 53.4(2) — the amount attributed to a family allowance recipient for more than one child, second additional contributory period` `the amounts determined under subsection (1), one for each child, calculated without regard to the other children` MEANS
    IF null `the amounts determined under subsection (1), one for each child, calculated without regard to the other children`
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE JUST (maximum `the amounts determined under subsection (1), one for each child, calculated without regard to the other children`)

-- src:1472 | (3) For the purposes of subsection (1), for a year in which the contributor’s second additional contributory period begins or ends, the amount to be attributed to the contributor is equal to that proportion of the amount determined in accordance with subsection (1) that the number of months that are included in the contributor’s second additional contributory period in that year is of 12.
@ref Act s 53.4(3) (src:1472)
GIVEN `the amount determined in accordance with subsection (1)` IS A NUMBER
      `the number of months included in the second additional contributory period in the year` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 53.4(3) — the amount attributed for a year in which the second additional contributory period begins or ends` `the amount determined in accordance with subsection (1)` `the number of months included in the second additional contributory period in the year` MEANS
    `the amount determined in accordance with subsection (1)` TIMES (`the number of months included in the second additional contributory period in the year` DIVIDED BY 12)

